{
  "case_id": "2020-19-1257",
  "document_hash": "eb2b04082193bdd9504dcae829d7cddd88684f276d5a06d69f85691af6d3867e",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2020-19-1257",
      "confidence": 0.97,
      "document_hash": "eb2b04082193bdd9504dcae829d7cddd88684f276d5a06d69f85691af6d3867e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-eb2b04082193-0000-0002",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 8,
        "start": 8
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Justice Alito delivered the opinion of the Court."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2020-19-1257",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "eb2b04082193bdd9504dcae829d7cddd88684f276d5a06d69f85691af6d3867e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-eb2b04082193-0001-0002",
      "kind": "holding",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 19,
        "start": 19
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Finally, the court found that the ballot-collection law had not been enacted with discriminatory intent. \u201c[T]he majority of H.B. 2023's proponents,\u201d the court found, \u201cwere sincere in their belief that ballot collection increased the risk of early voting fraud, and that H.B. 2023 was a necessary prophylactic measure to bring early mail ballot security in line with in-person voting.\u201d"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2020-19-1257",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "eb2b04082193bdd9504dcae829d7cddd88684f276d5a06d69f85691af6d3867e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-eb2b04082193-0002-0000",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "One judge in the majority declined to join the court's holding on discriminatory intent, and four others dissented across the board."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2020-19-1257",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "eb2b04082193bdd9504dcae829d7cddd88684f276d5a06d69f85691af6d3867e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-eb2b04082193-0002-0003",
      "kind": "holding",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We granted the petitions and agreed to review both the Ninth Circuit's understanding and application of VRA \u00a7 2 and its holding on discriminatory intent."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2020-19-1257",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "eb2b04082193bdd9504dcae829d7cddd88684f276d5a06d69f85691af6d3867e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-eb2b04082193-0002-0004",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Department informed us, however, that it did not dis- agree with its prior conclusion that the two provisions of Arizona law at issue in these cases do not violate \u00a7 2 of the Voting Rights Act."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2020-19-1257",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "eb2b04082193bdd9504dcae829d7cddd88684f276d5a06d69f85691af6d3867e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-eb2b04082193-0002-0006",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "First, the size of the burden imposed by a challenged voting rule is highly relevant."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2020-19-1257",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "eb2b04082193bdd9504dcae829d7cddd88684f276d5a06d69f85691af6d3867e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-eb2b04082193-0002-0007",
      "kind": "holding",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "One strong and entirely legitimate state interest is the prevention of fraud."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2020-19-1257",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "eb2b04082193bdd9504dcae829d7cddd88684f276d5a06d69f85691af6d3867e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-eb2b04082193-0003-0000",
      "kind": "holding",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 33,
        "start": 33
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In light of the principles set out above, neither Arizona's out-of-precinct rule nor its ballot-collection law violates \u00a7 2 of the VRA."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Carter-Baker Commission",
      "case_id": "2020-19-1257",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "eb2b04082193bdd9504dcae829d7cddd88684f276d5a06d69f85691af6d3867e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-eb2b04082193-0004-0003",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Carter-Baker Commission noted that \u201c[a]bsentee balloting is vulnerable to abuse in several ways: . . . . Citizens who vote at home, at nursing homes, at the workplace, or in church are more susceptible to pressure, overt and subtle, or to intimidation.\u201d"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2020-19-1257",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "eb2b04082193bdd9504dcae829d7cddd88684f276d5a06d69f85691af6d3867e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-eb2b04082193-0004-0000",
      "kind": "holding",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "As with the out-of-precinct policy, the modest evidence of racially disparate burdens caused by HB 2023, in light of the State's justifcations, leads us to the conclusion that the law does not violate \u00a7 2 of the VRA."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Democratic state senator",
      "case_id": "2020-19-1257",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "eb2b04082193bdd9504dcae829d7cddd88684f276d5a06d69f85691af6d3867e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-eb2b04082193-0004-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 43,
        "start": 43
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "One Democratic state senator pithily described the \u201c `problem' \u201d HB 2023 aimed to \u201c `solv[e]' \u201d as the fact that \u201c `one party is better at collecting ballots than the other one.' \u201d"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Proponents of the bill",
      "case_id": "2020-19-1257",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "eb2b04082193bdd9504dcae829d7cddd88684f276d5a06d69f85691af6d3867e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-eb2b04082193-0004-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 43,
        "start": 43
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Proponents of the bill repeatedly argued that mail-in ballots are more susceptible to fraud than in-person voting."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2020-19-1257",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "eb2b04082193bdd9504dcae829d7cddd88684f276d5a06d69f85691af6d3867e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-eb2b04082193-0004-0002",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Arizona's out-of-precinct policy and HB 2023 do not violate \u00a7 2 of the VRA, and HB 2023 was not enacted with a racially discriminatory purpose. The judgment of the Court of Appeals is reversed, and the cases are remanded for further proceedings consistent with this opinion."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2020-19-1257",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "eb2b04082193bdd9504dcae829d7cddd88684f276d5a06d69f85691af6d3867e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-eb2b04082193-0005-0000",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 49,
        "start": 49
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Momentous as the Fifteenth Amendment was, celebration of its achievements soon proved premature. The Amendment's guarantees \u201cquickly became dead letters in much of the country.\u201d"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2020-19-1257",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "eb2b04082193bdd9504dcae829d7cddd88684f276d5a06d69f85691af6d3867e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-eb2b04082193-0005-0001",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 52,
        "start": 52
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So Congress, in Section 5 of the Act, gave the Department of Justice authority to review all new rules devised by jurisdictions with a history of voter suppression\u2014and to block any that would have discriminatory effects."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2020-19-1257",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "eb2b04082193bdd9504dcae829d7cddd88684f276d5a06d69f85691af6d3867e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-eb2b04082193-0005-0002",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 54,
        "start": 54
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The most comprehensive study available found that in areas freed from Section 5 review, white turnout remained the same, but \u201cminority participation dropped by 2.1 percentage points\u201d\u2014a stark reversal in direction from prior elections."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2020-19-1257",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "eb2b04082193bdd9504dcae829d7cddd88684f276d5a06d69f85691af6d3867e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-eb2b04082193-0006-0000",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 59,
        "start": 59
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "\u201cbased on the totality of circumstances,\u201d a State's electoral system is \u201cnot equally open\u201d to members of a racial group."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2020-19-1257",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "eb2b04082193bdd9504dcae829d7cddd88684f276d5a06d69f85691af6d3867e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-eb2b04082193-0006-0001",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 60,
        "start": 60
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Suppose, as Justice Scalia once did, that a county has a law limiting \u201cvoter registration [to] only three hours one day a week.\u201d"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2020-19-1257",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "eb2b04082193bdd9504dcae829d7cddd88684f276d5a06d69f85691af6d3867e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-eb2b04082193-0006-0002",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 68,
        "start": 68
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Section 2 does not. What it cares about is that a State's \u201cpolitical processes\u201d are \u201cequally open\u201d to voters of all races."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2020-19-1257",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "eb2b04082193bdd9504dcae829d7cddd88684f276d5a06d69f85691af6d3867e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-eb2b04082193-0007-0000",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 70,
        "start": 70
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "That leaves only the majority's discussion of state interests, which is again skewed so as to limit Section 2 liability."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2020-19-1257",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "eb2b04082193bdd9504dcae829d7cddd88684f276d5a06d69f85691af6d3867e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-eb2b04082193-0008-0000",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 80,
        "start": 80
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "rural Arizona \u201coften must travel 45 minutes to 2 hours just to get to a mailbox.\u201d"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2020-19-1257",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "eb2b04082193bdd9504dcae829d7cddd88684f276d5a06d69f85691af6d3867e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-eb2b04082193-0008-0001",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 82,
        "start": 82
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Given those facts, the law prevents many Native Americans from making effective use of one of the principal means of voting in Arizona."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2020-19-1257",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "eb2b04082193bdd9504dcae829d7cddd88684f276d5a06d69f85691af6d3867e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-eb2b04082193-0008-0002",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 84,
        "start": 84
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the majority's treatment of the collection ban thus fouts what Section 2 commands: the eradication of election rules resulting in unequal opportunities for minority voters."
    }
  ],
  "schema_version": "1.0.0"
}
